applicable privacy and data-protection laws, including the LGPD when applicable.

7. Privacy And Data Protection Obligations

Any authorized operation, deployment, adaptation or derivative use that involves
personal data must be designed and operated with privacy and data protection in
mind. This includes, when applicable:

- identifying the applicable role of each party, including controller,
  operator/processor and any relevant service provider;
- defining a lawful basis or other legally valid justification for each data
  processing activity;
- collecting and processing only the data that is necessary for the authorized
  purpose;
- maintaining clear information for users about what data is processed, why it
  is processed, how long it is retained and how rights may be exercised;
- implementing reasonable technical and organizational security measures;
- keeping appropriate records of processing activities, logs and administrative
  access where legally or operationally required;
- defining retention and deletion rules for user, server, rank, economy, VIP,
  moderation, audit and log data;
- providing a process for user privacy requests where required by applicable
  law;
- establishing an incident response process for suspected or confirmed security
  incidents involving personal data;
- adopting appropriate contracts or data-processing terms with hosting,
  database, analytics, logging, API and infrastructure providers;
- applying special care when processing data related to children or
  adolescents, when applicable.

You may not export, copy, migrate, reuse or otherwise process data from the
official Hatsutech, Animes Cafe or copyright holder environments unless you have
separate, explicit written authorization to do so.

